cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "agent-payments: the proof bundle format"
message: >-
  If you use the agent-payments proof bundle format, please cite it using the
  metadata from this file. This is a specification: the reference
  implementations in this repository (Synsema, TypeScript and Rust) are
  distributed under the same terms and are not separately required.
type: standard
authors:
  - given-names: Joel
    family-names: Lucena
    alias: kitecosmic
    affiliation: Csibeings LLC
version: 0.1.0
date-released: '2026-11-23'
publisher:
  name: Csibeings LLC
repository-code: 'https://github.com/SYNSEMA/agent-payments'
url: 'https://github.com/SYNSEMA/agent-payments'
abstract: >-
  A portable, offline-verifiable evidence format for purchases made by AI
  agents. It binds what a user requested, what the agent proposed and what a
  human approved into a signed bundle that any third party can verify with
  public keys only - no network, no account, and no trust in the issuer. The
  reference implementation is written in Synsema; the reference verifiers are
  written in TypeScript and Rust and depend on nothing but their standard
  libraries.
keywords:
  - agentic-commerce
  - intent
  - verifiable-credentials
  - dispute-evidence
  - ap2
  - aep
  - conformance
  - webauthn
  - specification
license: Apache-2.0
